From 17edcaed2488fa3b88e4b7ae7da32e8c51fcae6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:21:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings: the Dolby Vision and HDR settings in groups, fewer
 of them at the default level

LibreELEC starts at the Advanced level, and about thirty settings of Hades were at
that level or below: the whole of Display > HDR was one list. Now:

- Display has four groups with a heading each: HDR (the brightness of the menus and
  the playback mode notice), Dolby Vision, HDR on displays without Dolby Vision and
  projectors, and HDR colour depth and format (advanced). A group with nothing at the
  level of the user does not show its heading.
- What only a person who tinkers would touch moves to Expert: the choice of 3D
  decoding and of the 3D output, BD-Live and the 3D simulation, HDR10 adapted to the
  display, Dolby Vision with HDR10+, the trims, the enhancement layer and HDR10+ of
  Dolby Vision as HDR10, its mapping to the display, the frame ahead and the fidelity
  step-down, and the audio settings about the downmix levels, the Dolby encoding, live
  passthrough and the dialogue normalisation. Nothing is removed and no value changes:
  a setting keeps what the user set, and a setting at a level that the user does not
  see keeps its default.
- The settings about what is sent to a display that takes Dolby Vision are shown only
  where the display declares it (new condition supportsdv, from the display
  information of the Dolby Vision decisions): a TV without Dolby Vision no longer
  lists them.
